`src/game.ts` exports `game`, a `GameDefinition<SpectraDebugApi>`: the game instance
class, a level registry holding the single level the game runs in, and `startLevel`
naming it. The game opens that one level and never opens another; every screen is a
value of the state's `screen` field, so the world and its game state live for the
whole session. The instance's `initialize` registers the actions, defines the cues,
