rules, and it adds a single player in its `beginPlay`, possessing nothing; that
player's controller is where the actions are read. The mode's `gameStateClass` is
`SpectraState`, so the world's game state is the state `specs/state.md` declares.
The actors, components, and controllers you write draw that state and drive it.

`src/game.ts` also declares and exports `SpectraState` and the types it is built
